    "text": "This solution is deliberately simple and conservative; I did not run it or check it against any data set.\n\nIt does two things:\n\n1. **Gifts within reach of the start.** Every gift whose location is within D of (0,0) is loaded and delivered immediately while the sleigh sits at the origin. This needs no carrots and no movement.\n2. **One one-way trip.** The remaining gifts are sorted by score, highest first. For each gift it searches for a trip of two accelerations: one along x, then one along y. The sleigh then floats until it is within D of the gift, and the program takes the first gift for which such a trip fits in the time limit T. It loads that gift plus 2 carrots, so the weight is w+2 at the first acceleration and w+1 at the second. Both accelerations are capped at the maximum for w+2, which is valid for both.\n\nBecause the search only uses speeds up to the sleigh's maximum acceleration, gifts that are very far away are skipped. Only one gift is delivered by the trip, and the sleigh does not return.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nint main(){\n    ll T,D;int W,G;\n    cin>>T>>D>>W>>G;\n    vector<ll> l(W),a(W);\n    for(int i=0;i<W;i++)cin>>l[i]>>a[i];\n    vector<string> nm(G);vector<ll> s(G),w(G),c(G),r(G);\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++)cin>>nm[i]>>s[i]>>w[i]>>c[i]>>r[i];\n    auto maxAcc=[&](ll wt)->ll{\n        for(int i=0;i<W;i++) if(wt<=l[i]) return a[i];\n        return 0;\n    };\n    vector<string> out;\n    vector<int> rest;\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++){\n        // c,r up to 1e9: squares up to 2e18 fits in ll (sum 2e18 < 9.2e18)\n        if(c[i]*c[i]+r[i]*r[i]<=D*D){\n            out.push_back(\"LoadGift \"+nm[i]);\n            out.push_back(\"DeliverGift \"+nm[i]);\n        } else rest.push_back(i);\n    }\n    sort(rest.begin(),rest.end(),[&](int x,int y){\n        if(s[x]!=s[y])return s[x]>s[y];\n        return x<y;\n    });\n    for(int gi:rest){\n        ll A=maxAcc(w[gi]+2);\n        if(A<=0)continue;\n        ll cc=c[gi],rr=r[gi];\n        ll t0=max((llabs(cc)+A-1)/A,(llabs(rr)+A-1)/A+1);\n        if(t0<2)t0=2;\n        bool found=false;\n        for(ll T1=t0;T1<=T&&!found;T1++){\n            ll s1=T1-1;\n            ll bx=llround((double)cc/T1), by=llround((double)rr/s1);\n            for(ll dx=-1;dx<=1&&!found;dx++)for(ll dy=-1;dy<=1&&!found;dy++){\n                ll vx=bx+dx,vy=by+dy;\n                if(llabs(vx)>A||llabs(vy)>A)continue;\n                ll px=vx*T1-cc,py=vy*s1-rr;\n                if(px*px+py*py<=D*D){\n                    found=true;\n                    out.push_back(\"LoadCarrots 2\");\n                    out.push_back(\"LoadGift \"+nm[gi]);\n                    if(vx>0)out.push_back(\"AccRight \"+to_string(vx));\n                    else if(vx<0)out.push_back(\"AccLeft \"+to_string(-vx));\n                    out.push_back(\"Float 1\");\n                    if(vy>0)out.push_back(\"AccUp \"+to_string(vy));\n                    else if(vy<0)out.push_back(\"AccDown \"+to_string(-vy));\n                    out.push_back(\"Float \"+to_string(s1));\n                    out.push_back(\"DeliverGift \"+nm[gi]);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        if(found)break;\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",(int)out.size());\n    for(auto&x:out)printf(\"%s\\n\",x.c_str());\n}\n```",
